        "scenario": "An owner sells closely held shares for $100,000 down and a $300,000 note over three years. Adjusted basis is disputed and sale documents allocate $30,000 to consulting.",
        "reading": "Integrated advanced legal examination. First identify the parties, forum, operative date and controlling legal authority. Create an issue tree with each required element, mark disputed and missing facts, and determine which side bears the burden. Draft a position for each side before selecting a reasoned outcome. Different doctrines require separate analyses even when a narrative connects them. Do not rely on the multiple-choice result as a grade for independent writing. Source citations must be verified against primary documents and later controlling developments.\n\nCase-specific analytical method: Begin with the actual scenario: An owner sells closely held shares for $100,000 down and a $300,000 note over three years. Adjusted basis is disputed and sale documents allocate $30,000 to consulting. Do not assume that the allegations are proven. List each actor, disputed fact, required evidentiary foundation, and burden of proof. Evaluate the strongest response: Taxpayer argues installment deferral; examiner contests basis substantiation and consulting allocation. Identify the exact proposition supported by IRC §§ 1001, 1012, 1221, 453 and applicable tax-year authorities, check whether that authority controls in the selected jurisdiction, and distinguish any conflicting or later decisions. Write a provisional conclusion conditioned on facts that remain unknown. Then change one material fact and explain whether the legal outcome would change. This exercise develops legal reasoning; neither a keyword match nor a quiz establishes mastery.",
